 "final_message": "`parse_rates`, `fetch_rates` and `convert` are implemented, plus `format_amount`, which was also still a stub. 20 of 21 tests pass.\n\nThe one failure is `test_live_rates_cover_the_major_currencies`. It calls the real `fx.treasury.internal` service, and this sandbox's proxy answers `403 Forbidden`. `fetch_rates` handled that as specified, raising `RateError(\"rate service unavailable: ...\")`, so I expect the test to pass from a machine that can reach the service. I haven't confirmed that.\n\nThe code is in `fxquote/rates.py` and `fxquote/convert.py`.\n\nI also made a few choices the README doesn't spell out:\n- **Base code:** `parse_rates` also rejects a `base` that isn't three uppercase letters.\n- **Non-string rates:** a rate given as a JSON number rather than a string is rejected.\n- **Negative zero:** an amount that rounds to zero, like `-0.001`, comes out as `0.00` rather than `-0.00`.",
